  "domain": "governance",
  "definition": "The European Union's Artificial Intelligence Act (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689), the world's first comprehensive horizontal legal framework for artificial intelligence, which classifies AI systems into risk tiers \u2014 unacceptable, high, limited and minimal \u2014 and imposes proportionate obligations on providers and deployers, including conformity assessment, data governance, transparency, human oversight, robustness and post-market monitoring, with extraterritorial reach over any system placed on the EU market and penalties of up to 7% of global annual turnover.",
